# Kestrel Agent Configuration
# Rules for Cline and other AI coding agents

## Project Context
- This is a Windows Event Log analyzer for SOC teams
- Backend: ASP.NET Core 8 (C#), Frontend: React 18 + TypeScript + Vite
- Database: SQLite with FTS5 search
- Detection: Custom Sigma rule matcher
- MITRE ATT&CK integration via embedded STIX JSON

## Code Rules
- Use async/await throughout the backend
- All API endpoints require authentication (cookie-based)
- Use server-side row streaming for AG Grid (100k+ rows)
- Never format event messages in the hot path (lazy rendering)
- Use Serilog structured logging for all operations
- All error handling: per-record, per-rule — never silent failures
- Use SQLite WAL mode
- HTTPS enforced in production

## Security Rules
- No unauthenticated access to event data
- Roles: Viewer / Analyst / Admin enforced server-side
- Upload validation: magic-byte check for EVTX files
- Background job parsing with timeout and memory bounds
- Input validation on all endpoints

## Architecture Patterns
- Backend uses background job queue for ingestion
- SignalR for real-time event push and alerts
- FTS5 trigram tokenizer for full-text search
- Sigma matcher: channel+EventID pre-filter → FastMatch → expression tree evaluation
- Evtx parsing via System.Diagnostics.Eventing.Reader
- Docker deployment with nginx TLS termination

## Do Not
- Do NOT use Blazor for the frontend — use React
- Do NOT use JWT/localStorage for auth — use cookies + SameSite
- Do NOT use browser-side (WASM) parsing — server-side only
- Do NOT use Lucene.NET — use SQLite FTS5
- Do NOT allow unauthenticated localhost binding in production
